From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:45:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/87] web-app: keep Copy Selection available on caption-less
 messages

The context menu's copy entry ("Copy Text"/"Copy Selection"/"Copy
Email") was gated on the message having its own text: `text !== '' &&
copy_item`. An image (or any attachment) with no caption has
`text === ''`, so the entry vanished entirely -- including "Copy
Selection", even when the right-click landed on a text selection made
elsewhere in the bubble, e.g. inside a quoted message. Selecting a
quote's text and copying it from a caption-less image stopped working.

Gate on there being something to copy instead: a live selection, a
clicked email, or non-empty message text. A caption still hides the
entry once none of the three apply, same as before.
---
 packages/frontend/src/components/message/Message.tsx | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/message/Message.tsx b/packages/frontend/src/components/message/Message.tsx
index 9ebcadb..0f72152 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/message/Message.tsx
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/message/Message.tsx
@@ -437,8 +437,9 @@ function buildContextMenu(
         label: tx('menu_copy_link_to_clipboard'),
         action: () => runtime.writeClipboardText(link),
       },
-    // copy item (selection or all text)
-    text !== '' && copy_item,
+    // copy item (selection, email, or all text) — a caption-less image can
+    // still have a selection worth copying, e.g. from a quoted message.
+    (textSelected || Boolean(email) || text !== '') && copy_item,
     // Copy image
     showCopyImage && {
       label: tx('menu_copy_image_to_clipboard'),
